PHYSICS + FX

Impact Physics: Every mech movement generates micro-shockwaves. Ground trembles. Trash, dust, stickers, and graffiti flakes scatter directionally. Footsteps compress surfaces and kick debris.

Air/Fluid Dynamics: High-speed dodges create wake turbulence and heat distortions. Drone swarm generates vortex swirls. Rain curves around motion trajectories.

Micro-Particles: Persistent neon grime and dust float in the alley, reacting dynamically to character movement. Time-slice shots freeze all particles perfectly.

Mech FX: Torque flex on servos, vibrating plates, oily steam jets, glowing rotating eye lenses, hydraulic recoil, metal fatigue groans.

Energy FX: Concentric rotating rings inside the mech’s eye, arc sparks, electrical discharges affecting nearby neon signs. Kid’s punch emits blue-white power bloom with short afterimage streaking.

Destruction FX: Falling neon signs with glass shattering, concrete splintering, small craters on impacts, trash bags bursting with soft-body physics.

Environmental Light Reaction: Neon reflections animate across wet ground; pink mech light casts moving reflections; dust clouds glow when hit by beam energy; volumetric light tunnels.

Cloth & Body Physics: Jacket flapping, hood strings with spring dynamics, short lagging straps, compression of boots, proper anticipation/recoil in punches and landings.

Camera Physics: Hand-held realism, micro-shake on shockwaves, whip-pans, smooth stabilization during slow-mo, rebound after big impacts.

Time-Slice FX: Particles suspended mid-air, frozen debris, static beam energy interior flicker, camera moves freely while world is frozen.

CAMERA RULES

Always moving · expressive · hand-held · no static tripod shots · whip-pans · reverse dolly · orbit shots · slow-motion beats · hard-shake on impacts · proximity changes to emphasize scale.

